thodInvestmentAggregateCost" scale="9" id="Narr_VrP0N3vfY0KErfGONkym_A">1</ix:nonFraction>&#160;billion in June&#160;2017. This round of equity financing was initially conducted by increasing registered capital of Shenzhen Xiaoying by 9 existing and new investors. Subsequently, X Financial issued additional shares to the affiliates of the same shareholders of this round of equity financing such that the shareholder ownership in X Financial mirrored those in Shenzhen Xiaoying.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:36pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">The Group considered the Reorganization as a reorganization of entities under common control. Accordingly, the accompanying financial statements have been prepared using historical cost basis.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:36pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">During December&#160;2017, Beijing WFOE acquired <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_subsidiary_UC9KMrWjUUaSIbiCOvsj3Q" contextRef="Duration_12_1_2017_To_12_31_2017_dei_LegalEntityAxis_xyf_XiaoyingBeijingInformationTechnologyCoLtdMember_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_xyf_ShenzhenXiaoyingTechnologyCoLtdMember_wsEghxxlzUeVs9gcz0mYRA" decimals="0" format="ixt-sec:numwordsen" name="xyf:NumberOfSubsidiariesAcquired" scale="0" id="Narr_k4vdngwZyUK9Gx-9PphOJw">two</ix:nonFraction> subsidiaries from Shenzhen Xiaoying at cost. During February and March 2018, one of the Group&#8217;s wholly-owned subsidiaries Shenzhen Xiaoying Puhui Technology Co., Ltd. (&#8220;Shenzhen Puhui&#8221;) acquired <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_subsidiary_UC9KMrWjUUaSIbiCOvsj3Q" contextRef="Duration_2_1_2018_To_3_31_2018_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_xyf_ShenzhenYingZhongTongFinancialInformationServiceCoLtdMember_srt_OwnershipAxis_xyf_ShenzhenXiaoyingPuhuiTechnologyCoLtdMember__O3GXd7H60S9R0pzIfeYjQ" decimals="0" format="ixt-sec:numwordsen" name="xyf:NumberOfSubsidiariesAcquired" scale="0" id="Narr_07_OafopoEO6vjm0dWofpg">four</ix:nonFraction> subsidiaries from one of the VIE entities Shenzhen Ying Zhong Tong at cost. During 2018, predominantly all of the SPVs under Shenzhen Xiaoying had been transferred to Shenzhen Xiaoying Puhui Technology Co., Ltd. These transactions represented a reorganization of entities under common control as they were already within the consolidated Group, with no impact to the consolidated financials.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:36pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">In September 2018, the Group completed an initial public offering of <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_shares_NMqbQ0zKMUm5UWX49YbyhQ" contextRef="Duration_9_1_2018_To_9_30_2018_us-gaap_StatementClassOfStockAxis_dei_AdrMember_us-gaap_SubsidiarySaleOfStockAxis_us-gaap_IPOMember_OBcfFCZ-P022fa5vM5W_fw" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:StockIssuedDuringPeriodSharesNewIssues" scale="0" id="Narr_Z6r7g0EoBUe-uqw9O6vaSw">11,763,478</ix:nonFraction> American depositary shares (&#8220;ADSs&#8221;) at an initial offering price of US$<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Divide_USD_shares_bIx1MrBb80OPhGT_fNi7bA" contextRef="As_Of_9_30_2018_us-gaap_StatementClassOfStockAxis_dei_AdrMember_us-gaap_SubsidiarySaleOfStockAxis_us-gaap_IPOMember_vosSvbJu2kukHB1GecU7ZA" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:SharesIssuedPricePerShare" scale="0" id="Narr_8WQAt1Ca3ke_QH7ePgCN8Q">9.50</ix:nonFraction> which included the ADSs sold upon the exercise of the over-allotment option granted to the underwriters, representing <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_shares_NMqbQ0zKMUm5UWX49YbyhQ" contextRef="Duration_9_1_2018_To_9_30_2018_us-gaap_StatementClassOfStockAxis_us-gaap_CommonClassAMember_us-gaap_SubsidiarySaleOfStockAxis_us-gaap_IPOMember_HpvAH5ZLOk-w14j820dyXA" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:StockIssuedDuringPeriodSharesNewIssues" scale="0" id="Narr_8lYaxydZvUqG_be2TWM7xw">23,526,956</ix:nonFraction> Class A ordinary shares. Effective from November 19, 2020, the ratio of ADSs representing the Class A ordinary shares changed from one (1) ADS representing two (2) Class A ordinary shares to one (1) ADS representing six (6) Class A ordinary shares.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:36pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">On May 31, 2021, Shenzhen Quanbei Microcredit Co., Ltd. (&#8220;Quanbei Microcredit&#8221;, formerly known as &#8220;Shenzhen Xiaoying Microcredit Co., Ltd.&#8221;) was incorporated in the Chinese Mainland with online microcredit business operating license by Shenzhen Xiaoying. Shenzhen Xiaoying had completed the capital contributions of RMB<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_YQYnjBUfVkKlgHZPDi4wHw" contextRef="Duration_11_1_2021_To_11_30_2021_srt_ConsolidatedEntitiesAxis_xyf_ShenzhenQuanbeiMicrocreditCoLtdMember_SWBX4vZwxEusY1xRTW0Pvg" decimals="-9" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="xyf:CapitalContribution" scale="9" id="Narr_eOzinM0R7k-btr-f25bvng">1</ix:nonFraction> billion to Quanbei Microcredit in November, 2021.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:36pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">On May 20, 2022, Tianjin Yuexin Financing Guarantee Co., Ltd. (&#8220;Tianjin Yuexin&#8221;) was incorporated in the Chinese Mainland with financing guarantee license by Shenzhen Puhui. Shenzhen Puhui had completed the capital contributions of RMB<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_YQYnjBUfVkKlgHZPDi4wHw" contextRef="Duration_5_20_2022_To_5_20_2022_srt_ConsolidatedEntitiesAxis_xyf_TianjinYuexinFinancingGuaranteeCoLtdMember_K4K3XCm5jka7xw_dqZL8zA" decimals="-6" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="xyf:CapitalContribution" scale="6" id="Narr_D0e_dlI2-0Sq3VQ-DPGxUw">50</ix:nonFraction> million to Tianjin Yuexin in 2022. By the end of December 2023, the registered capital of Tianjin Yuexin was increased to RMB<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_YQYnjBUfVkKlgHZPDi4wHw" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2023_srt_ConsolidatedEntitiesAxis_xyf_TianjinYuexinFinancingGuaranteeCoLtdMember_smLOp5huskGGxJgoOGhiLQ" decimals="-9" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="xyf:RegisteredCapital" scale="9" id="Narr_kTHqRiJW5k-6P8fS1oFOJw">1</ix:nonFraction> billion.</p><ix:nonNumeric contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_Yy6Jg489uEiAjI1FBjE_Pg" name="xyf:ScheduleOfSubsidiariesVariableInterestEntitiesAndSubsidiariesOfVariableInterestEntitiesTableTextBlock" id="Tb_H1gMHu7NbEqVz-EWM6vSNw" escape="true"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:36pt;margin:0pt;">As of December 31, 2025, the Company&#8217;s principal subsidiaries, VIEs and subsidiaries of the VIEs are as follows:</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="margin-bottom:12pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><table style="border-collapse:collapse;font-size:16pt;height:max-content;margin-left:auto;margin-right:auto;padding-left:0pt;padding-right:0pt;width:100%;"><tr style="height:1pt;"><td style="vertical-align:bottom;width:41.89%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><div style="height:1pt;overflow:hidden;overflow-wrap:break-word;position:relative;"><div style="bottom:0pt;position:absolute;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:1pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></div></div></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:1.48%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><div style="height:1pt;overflow:hidden;overflow-wrap:break-word;position:relative;"><div style="bottom:0pt;position:absolute;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:1pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></div></div></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:11.81%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><div style="height:1pt;overflow:hidde