itsAdvancedFromOwnFundsPolicyPolicyTextBlock" id="Tb_ohhERw25Qk-x2ekQYQUuUg" continuedAt="Tb_ohhERw25Qk-x2ekQYQUuUg_cont1" escape="true"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:bold;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 36pt;"><span style="display:inline-block;text-indent:0pt;width:36pt;"><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:bold;">(m)</span></span>Loans receivables from Xiaoying Credit Loans and other loans, net</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:36pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">Loans receivables represent loans facilitated through the Consolidated Trusts and Partnerships and loans provided by Quanbei Microcredit, which consist of Xiaoying Credit Loans, Xiaoying Revolving Loans which ceased to be facilitated as of 2020, and other miscellaneous loans that the Group facilitated and originated during the years. Loans receivables from Xiaoying Credit Loans and other loans are stated at the historical carrying amount net of write-offs and allowance for credit losses. The Group establishes an allowance for credit losses in accordance with ASC Topic 326 based on estimates, historical experience of net vintage-based loss rates, current economic conditions, reasonable and supportable forecasts of future economic conditions and other factors surrounding the credit risk of borrowers. The profile of the borrowers is similar under each product therefore the Group applies a consistent credit risk management framework to the entire portfolio of borrowers under each product. The Group evaluates and adjusts its allowance for credit losses for loans receivables on a quarterly basis or more often as necessary. Uncollectible loans receivables are charged off when a settlement is reached for an amount that is less than the outstanding balance or when loans receivables are deemed uncollectible.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:36pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">As of December 31, 2024 and 2025, loans receivables from Xiaoying Credit Loans and other loans amounted to RMB<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_YQYnjBUfVkKlgHZPDi4wHw" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2024_xyf_MajorProductsAxis_xyf_XiaoyingCreditLoansAndOtherLoansMember_cNJS8DtQj0KGL7lgqCSrtg" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:NotesReceivableNet" scale="0" id="Narr_Kru5F2buhEmlm6riYeLykA">4,828,316,995</ix:nonFraction> and RMB<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_YQYnjBUfVkKlgHZPDi4wHw" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2025_xyf_MajorProductsAxis_xyf_XiaoyingCreditLoansAndOtherLoansMember_MemOE-sMKEy7kAI0GkxOEA" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:NotesReceivableNet" scale="0" id="Narr_hxRlHWSIF0663KeT4qRVxA">5,298,631,388</ix:nonFraction> (US$<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_mso-ZoIOikybqHvJnzvpJA" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2025_xyf_MajorProductsAxis_xyf_XiaoyingCreditLoansAndOtherLoansMember_MemOE-sMKEy7kAI0GkxOEA" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:NotesReceivableNet" scale="0" id="Narr_ME8G5CGfcEyQzy08wCYSNg">757,694,211</ix:nonFraction>) respectively. The general life time of loans receivables from Xiaoying Credit Loans and other loans lasts no more than 12 months.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:36pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">The Group excluded the accrued interest receivable balance, net of allowance for credit loss, from the disclosed amortized cost basis, amounting to RMB<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_YQYnjBUfVkKlgHZPDi4wHw" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2024_8BnYgVflKke7ghe7mN0nCA" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="xyf:LoansReceivableAccruedInterest" scale="0" id="Narr_RZC08m6peEinyt8PuZpZ5Q">71,667,521</ix:nonFraction> and RMB<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_YQYnjBUfVkKlgHZPDi4wHw" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2025_JPSOWL18b0mRymlbaD