:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">In 2021 and 2022, the Group recorded dividend receivable of RMB<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_YQYnjBUfVkKlgHZPDi4wHw" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2021_To_12_31_2021_sztqKwLdjEaTDq_yaYnd9A" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="xyf:DividendReceivable" scale="0" id="Narr__G9kmpZDyEWXGSZ3Nuiv_A"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_YQYnjBUfVkKlgHZPDi4wHw" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2022_To_12_31_2022_T0TdMIu-LkK6TDk3HsSZXg" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="xyf:DividendReceivable" scale="0" id="Narr_UgUrBcEH60GS0VCFZtTg_w">15,000,000</ix:nonFraction></ix:nonFraction>, and collected the amount in 2023, from the nominal shareholder of Jiangxi Ruijing, the nominal shareholder is controlled by Mr. Yue (Justin) Tang. In 2024 and 2025, the Group received dividend of RMB<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_YQYnjBUfVkKlgHZPDi4wHw" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2024_To_12_31_2024_kw0CL7RuNkCBgChw00bupA" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:InvestmentIncomeDividend" scale="0" id="Narr_6IIQxwNw00emdkPf8_1ycA">7,500,000</ix:nonFraction> and RMB<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_YQYnjBUfVkKlgHZPDi4wHw" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_Yy6Jg489uEiAjI1FBjE_Pg" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:InvestmentIncomeDividend" scale="0" id="Narr_s_YXw_JqM0CyIa-4Fljcdw">15,000,000</ix:nonFraction> from the nominal shareholder of Jiangxi Ruijing.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:36pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">In 2022, the Group entered into agreements with Newup Bank of Liaoning (&#8220;Newup Bank&#8221;), according to which the Group charged service fees directly to Newup Bank for the intermediary service the Group provided. The Group recognized total net revenue of RMB<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_YQYnjBUfVkKlgHZPDi4wHw" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2023_To_12_31_2023_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_xyf_NewupBankOfLiaoningMember_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionsByRelatedPartyAxis_us-gaap_OtherAffiliatesMember_7ZY682IsvEyTOP4jOUmQ_w" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:Revenues" scale="0" id="Narr_u1GeiY_Zh0KMP2qTEvSTiQ">11,370,044</ix:nonFraction> during the year of 2023 in connection with the service fees of facilitation service for loans. Accounts receivable and contract assets amounted to RMB<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_YQYnjBUfVkKlgHZPDi4wHw" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2023_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_xyf_NewupBankOfLiaoningMember_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionsByRelatedPartyAxis_us-gaap_OtherAffiliatesMember_eJvvv4-hu0u-lhyBK0cNeg" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:ContractWithCustomerAssetNet" scale="0" id="Narr_swE0P4dkWUew-fYcMHnOJg">1,096,251</ix:nonFraction> with respect to December 31, 2023, which had been fully settled in 2024.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:36pt;margin:0pt;">The terms of the agreements with the related parties are determined based on contracted prices negotiated with other parties in normal commercial terms.</p></ix:nonNumeric><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></div><div style="clear:both;padding-bottom:36pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:24pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;">F-48</p></div></div>
<div style="background-color:#000000;clear:both;height:2pt;page-break-after:always;width:88.24%;border:0;margin:30pt 5.88% 30pt 5.88%;"></div><div style="margin-left:5.88%;margin-right:5.88%;max-width:100%;position:relative;"><div style="padding-top:21.6pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 30pt 0pt;"><a href="#TOC"><span style="font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">Table of Contents</span></a></p></div><div style="clear:both;max-width:100%;position:relative;"><ix:nonNumeric contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_Yy6Jg489uEiAjI1FBjE_Pg" name="us-gaap:IncomeTaxDisclosureTextBlock" id="Tb_gRnnKKlG2kmGnhtyqK0ymA" continuedAt="Tb_gRnnKKlG2kmGnhtyqK0ymA_cont1" escape="true"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;margin:0pt 0pt 10pt 36pt;">14. Income taxes</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;margin:0pt 0pt 10pt 36pt;">Cayman Islands</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:36pt;margin:0pt 0pt 10pt 0pt;">X Financial is a company incorporated in the Cayman Islands. Under the current laws of the Cayman Islands, the Company is not subject to tax on either income or capital gain.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;margin:0pt 0pt 10pt 36pt;">Hong Kong</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:36pt;margin:0pt 0pt 10pt 0pt;">Under the current Hong Kong Inland Revenue Ordinance, YZT (HK) Limited and YX (HK) Limited, subsidiaries of the Group located in Hong Kong, are subject to a two-tiered profits tax rates for taxable income earned in Hong Kong for the years ended December 31, 2023, 2024 and 2025. The first HK$<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_HKD_KrKalp-D40W0nb011Qtm1g" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_srt_StatementGeographicalAxis_country_HK_14CzZWS30UWGe6u1BgWowg" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="xyf:ThresholdProfitsInDeterminingTaxRate" scale="6" id="Narr_26pAGcu8hkafP7Z7JgLT_w">2.0</ix:nonFraction> million Hong Kong dollars of profits earned by a company are subject to be taxed at an income tax rate at <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_OwgFp_vI5E2XKafnnhSnew" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2023_To_12_31_2023_srt_StatementGeographicalAxis_country_HK_srt_StatementScenarioAxis_xyf_First2MillionHkdOfProfitEarnedByCompanyMember_3xPfRchKGU6lCYG1L9VfEA" decimals="4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:EffectiveIncomeTaxRateReconciliationAtFederalStatutoryIncomeTaxRate" scale="-2" id="Narr_Lb_jm6VcWUyhGjd7fZLdbg"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_OwgFp_vI5E2XKafnnhSnew" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2024_To_12_31_2024_srt_StatementGeographicalAxis_country_HK_srt_StatementScenarioAxis_xyf_First2MillionHkdOfProfitEarnedByCompanyMember_l3ZvaAxMA0aPv7TsDRGvuQ" decimals="4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:EffectiveIncomeTaxRateReconciliationAtFederalStatutoryIncomeTaxRate" scale="-2" id="Narr_8ElJljXQfUOYY8qeYOz-oA"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_OwgFp_vI5E2XKafnnhSnew" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_srt_StatementGeographicalAxis_country_HK_srt_StatementScenarioAxis_xyf_First2MillionHkdOfProfitEarnedByCompanyMember_dEb9NPICnEe2JnzJHjBnBg" decimals="4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:EffectiveIncomeTaxRateReconciliationAtFederalStatutoryIncomeTaxRate" scale="-2" id="Narr_25hyFTyd20KmQAYeMxhSEg">8.25</ix:nonFraction></ix:nonFraction></ix:nonFraction>%, while the remaining profits will continue to be taxed at the existing tax rate, <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_OwgFp_vI5E2XKafnnhSnew" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2023_To_12_31_2023_srt_StatementGeographicalAxis_country_HK_srt_StatementScenarioAxis_xyf_ProfitEarnedByCompanyExceedingFirst2MillionHkdMember_wv6XdyAAf0yPua4lr6NXqw" decimals="3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:EffectiveIncomeTaxRateReconciliationAtFederalStatutoryIncomeTaxRate" scale="-2" id="Narr_Q2pZRBAZ_kaYnY_xcguC8w"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_OwgFp_vI5E2XKafnnhSnew" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2024_To_12_31_2024_srt_StatementGeographicalAxis_country_HK_srt_StatementScenarioAxis_xyf_ProfitEarnedByCompanyExceedingFirst2MillionHkdMember_7onUnrLAC0aYn9oQTL0uNQ" decimals="3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:EffectiveIncomeTaxRateReconciliationAtFederalStatutoryIncomeTaxRate" scale="-2" id="Narr_osXwYG7f1UuCOwxmLoxLwg">16.5</ix:nonFraction></ix:nonFraction>%. No income tax expense for these entities has been recognized in the consolidated financial statements as they have no assessable income for the years ended December 31, 2023 and 2024. For the year ended December 31, 2025, the income tax expense recognized for these entities was immaterial. </p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:36pt;margin:0pt 0pt 10pt 0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;">Chinese Mainland</b></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:36pt;margin:0pt 0pt 10pt 0pt;">Under the Law of the PRC on Enterprise Income Tax (the &#8220;EIT Law&#8221;), the Company&#8217;s subsidiaries, VIEs and subsidiaries of the VIEs established in the Chinese Mainland are subject to an income tax rate of <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_OwgFp_vI5E2XKafnnhSnew" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_srt_StatementGeographicalAxis_country_CN_PiXgZ5sZokmpluX0YZKM-Q" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:EffectiveIncomeTaxRateReconciliationAtFederalStatutoryIncomeTaxRate" scale="-2" id="Narr_Ksi8UJSAFkyVJVie9kAfLw">25</ix:nonFraction>% for the years presented. However, certain entities are eligible for preferential tax treatments. Specifically, one subsidiary is granted a <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_OwgFp_vI5E2XKafnnhSnew" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_xyf_StatusForTaxabilityAxis_xyf_QualifiedEnterpriseMember_rxCW4wJkyUSztLKJd2wjsg" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:EffectiveIncomeTaxRateReconciliationAtFederalStatutoryIncomeTaxRate" scale="-2" id="Narr_XiPatw_D202MLwQHsXJeAA">15</ix:nonFraction>% preferential income tax rate as a qualified enterprise under an incentive regime through 2027. Additionally, under a different incentive regime, <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_OwgFp_vI5E2XKafnnhSnew" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_Yy6Jg489uEiAjI1FBjE_Pg" decimals="0" format="ixt-sec:numwordsen" name="xyf:NumberOfSubsidiary" scale="0" id="Narr_cRB_6n3mvkKT6SS96jcjJw">one</ix:nonFraction> VIE and two other subsidiaries, operating in a specific preferential tax jurisdiction, are subject to a reduced income tax rate of <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_OwgFp_vI5E2XKafnnhSnew" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_us-gaap_TaxPeriodAxis_xyf_TaxYear2020To2025Member_xyf_StatusForTaxabilityAxis_xyf_QualifiedEnterpriseMember_64_QcP3hJE-cRgPjMjHGGQ" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="xyf:PercentageOfSubjectToReducedEnterpriseIncomeTaxRate" scale="-2" id="Narr_ne214CKYd0-lY_8_f3zn6Q">15</ix:nonFraction>% through 2027; of these two subsidiaries, one became eligible for such reduced tax rate starting from 2025. Furthermore, a subsidiary established in 2025, operating in another specific preferential tax jurisdiction, was eligible for a reduced income tax rate of <span style="-sec-ix-hidden:Hidden_G38TOq9K0U6cg7e1WNRQ6g;"><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">15%</span></span> through 2030.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:36pt;margin:0pt 0pt 10pt 0pt;">Uncertainties exist with respect to how the current income tax law in the Chinese Mainland applies to the Group&#8217;s overall operations, and more specifically, with regard to its tax residency status. The EIT Law includes a provision specifying that legal entities organized outside of the Chinese Mainland will be considered residents for Chinese Income Tax purposes if the place of effective management or control is within the Chinese Mainland. The implementation rules to the EIT Law provide that non-resident legal entities will be considered Chinese Mainland residents if substantial and overall management and control over the manufacturing and business operations, personnel, accounting and properties, occurs within the Chinese Mainland. Despite the present uncertainties resulting from the limited Chinese Mainland tax guidance on the issue, the Group does not believe that the legal entities organized outside of the Chinese Mainland within the Group should be treated as residents for EIT Law purposes and, therefore, has not recorded an unrecognized tax benefit for this tax position. If the Chinese Mainland taxing authorities subsequently determine that the Company and its subsidiaries registered outside the Chinese Mainland should be deemed resident enterprises, the Company and its subsidiaries registered outside the Chinese Mainland would be subject to Chinese Mainland income taxes, at a statutory income tax rate of <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_OwgFp_vI5E2XKafnnhSnew" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_Yy6Jg489uEiAjI1FBjE_Pg" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:EffectiveIncomeTaxRateReconciliationAtFederalStatutoryIncomeTaxRate" scale="-2" id="Narr_rhGVZEla5k-TaQCOMedZDA">25</ix:nonFraction>%.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:36pt;margin:0pt 0pt 10pt 0pt;">According to PRC Administration of the Levy and Collection of Taxes Law, the statute of limitations is <ix:nonNumeric contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_srt_StatementGeographicalAxis_country_CN_PiXgZ5sZokmpluX0YZKM-Q" format="ixt-sec:durwordsen" name="xyf:IncomeTaxStatuteOfLimitationsPeriod" id="Narr_Y---HWIoHEOJSwovVlV3SQ">three&#160;years</ix:nonNumeric> if an underpayment of taxes is due to computational errors made by the taxpayer or withholding agent. The statute of limitations will be extended <ix:nonNumeric contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_srt_StatementGeographicalAxis_country_CN_PiXgZ5sZokmpluX0YZKM-Q" format="ixt-sec:durwordsen" name="xyf:IncomeTaxStatuteOfLimitationsExtensionPeriodUnderSpecialCircumstances" id="Narr__hTod72Ds0Gg03SqPUOPAA">five&#160;years</ix:nonNumeric> under special circumstances, which are not clearly defined (but an underpayment of tax liability exceeding RMB<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_YQYnjBUfVkKlgHZPDi4wHw" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2025_srt_StatementGeographicalAxis_country_CN_SgSXiQt2B022j19mdWVfaQ" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="xyf:IncomeTaxUnderpaymentOfTaxLiabilityListedInSpecialCircumstances" scale="6" id="Narr_9-44EKCRJU6kVxgDI79dVA">0.1</ix:nonFraction>&#160;million is specifically listed as a special circumstance). In the case of a related party transaction, the statute of limitations is <ix:nonNumeric contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_srt_StatementGeographicalAxis_country_CN_PiXgZ5sZokmpluX0YZKM-Q" format="ixt-sec:durwordsen" name="xyf:IncomeTaxStatuteOfLimitationsRelatedPartyTransactionPeriod" id="Narr_tIvaAx-u6U-CU1KgXjpnRQ">ten&#160;years</ix:nonNumeric>. There is <span style="-sec-ix-hidden:Hidden_-TEbf5OL_kOtiuq4mlMMcw;"><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">no</span></span> statute of limitations in the case of tax evasion. Tax years from 2015 to the current year for the Group&#8217;s Chinese Mainland subsidiaries are subject to examination by the Chinese Mainland taxing authorities.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></ix:nonNumeric></div><div style="clear:both;padding-bottom:3