<div style="background-color:#000000;clear:both;height:2pt;page-break-after:always;width:88.24%;border:0;margin:30pt 5.88% 30pt 5.88%;"></div><div style="margin-left:5.88%;margin-right:5.88%;max-width:100%;position:relative;"><div style="padding-top:21.6pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 30pt 0pt;"><a href="#TOC"><span style="font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">Table of Contents</span></a></p></div><div style="clear:both;max-width:100%;position:relative;"><ix:nonNumeric contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_Yy6Jg489uEiAjI1FBjE_Pg" name="xyf:StatutoryReservesAndRestrictedNetAssetsTextBlock" id="Tb_ewVKNtaTQUieYJUUi2J0kQ" escape="true"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 36pt;">17. Statutory reserves and restricted net assets</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:36pt;margin:0pt 0pt 10pt 0pt;">The Company&#8217;s ability to pay dividends is primarily dependent on the Company receiving distributions of funds from its subsidiaries. Relevant Chinese Mainland statutory laws and regulations permit payments of dividends by the VIEs and subsidiaries of the VIEs incorporated in Chinese Mainland only out of their retained earnings, if any, as determined in accordance with Chinese Mainland accounting standards and regulations. The consolidated results of operations reflected in the consolidated financial statements prepared in accordance with U.S. GAAP differ from those reflected in the statutory financial statements of the Company&#8217;s subsidiaries.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:36pt;margin:0pt 0pt 10pt 0pt;">Under Chinese Mainland law, the Company&#8217;s subsidiaries, VIEs and the subsidiaries of the VIEs located in the Chinese Mainland (collectively referred as the &#8220;Chinese Mainland entities&#8221;) are required to provide for certain statutory reserves, namely a general reserve, an enterprise expansion fund and a staff welfare and bonus fund. The Chinese Mainland entities are required to allocate at least <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_OwgFp_vI5E2XKafnnhSnew" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_Yy6Jg489uEiAjI1FBjE_Pg" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="xyf:MinimumPercentageOfAfterTaxProfitToBeAllocatedToStatutoryReserve" scale="-2" id="Narr_QEsqznHm1Ey6rpxhpxRLhg">10</ix:nonFraction>% of their after tax profits on an individual company basis as determined under Chinese Mainland accounting standards to the statutory reserve and has the right to discontinue allocations to the statutory reserve if such reserve has reached <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_OwgFp_vI5E2XKafnnhSnew" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_Yy6Jg489uEiAjI1FBjE_Pg" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="xyf:RequiredStatutoryReserveRegisteredCapitalRatioToDeforceCompulsoryNetProfitAllocationToStatutoryReserve" scale="-2" id="Narr_9A4CxytfG0akhmJo1SaKbw">50</ix:nonFraction>% of registered capital on an individual company basis. In addition, the registered capital of the Chinese Mainland entities is also restricted.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:36pt;margin:0pt;">Amounts restricted that include paid-in capital, additional paid-in capital and statutory reserve funds, as determined pursuant to China Accounting Standard, are RMB<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_YQYnjBUfVkKlgHZPDi4wHw" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2024_8BnYgVflKke7ghe7mN0nCA" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="xyf:AmountsRestrictedWhichIncludesPaidInCapitalAdditionalPaidInCapitalAndStatutoryReserveFund" scale="0" id="Narr_vE4CxNKtpkKbwbD5Yw6kgA">4,816,033,362</ix:nonFraction> and RMB<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_YQYnjBUfVkKlgHZPDi4wHw" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2025_JPSOWL18b0mRymlbaDz_Xg" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="xyf:AmountsRestrictedWhichIncludesPaidInCapitalAdditionalPaidInCapitalAndStatutoryReserveFund" scale="0" id="Narr_uw6CePGOHEiiz03VfUVbag">5,046,425,864</ix:nonFraction> (US$<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_mso-ZoIOikybqHvJnzvpJA" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2025_JPSOWL18b0mRymlbaDz_Xg" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="xyf:AmountsRestrictedWhichIncludesPaidInCapitalAdditionalPaidInCapitalAndStatutoryReserveFund" scale="0" id="Narr_dKIQ9RX3YUqA1MljRhoXqQ">721,629,301</ix:nonFraction>) as of December 31, 2024 and 2025 respectively. </p></ix:nonNumeric><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:36pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="margin-bottom:12pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><ix:nonNumeric contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_Yy6Jg489uEiAjI1FBjE_Pg" name="us-gaap:CommitmentsAndContingenciesDisclosureTextBlock" id="Tb_m0_je74_Rka8TtegYju2PQ" escape="true"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 36pt;">18. Commitments and contingencies</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 10pt 36pt;"><span style="text-decoration-color:#000000;text-decoration-line:underline;text-decoration-style:solid;">Contingencies</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:36pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">The Group is subject to periodic legal or administrative proceedings in the ordinary course of business. The Group does not have any pending legal or administrative proceeding to which the Group is a party that will have a material effect on its business or financial condition.</p></ix:nonNumeric><ix:nonNumeric contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_Yy6Jg489uEiAjI1FBjE_Pg" name="us-gaap:SubsequentEventsTextBlock" id="Tb_PBt9gmhXy0OpxpTtFOjCUw" continuedAt="Tb_PBt9gmhXy0OpxpTtFOjCUw_cont1" escape="true"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 36pt;">19. Subsequent events</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:36pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">In first quarter of 2026, the Group has drawn down several short-term borrowings in aggregation amounting to RMB<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_YQYnjBUfVkKlgHZPDi4wHw" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2026_To_3_31_2026_us-gaap_SubsequentEventTypeAxis_us-gaap_SubsequentEventMember_jGGebv-Vt0OAcmopqfvB2w" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:ProceedsFromShortTermDebt" scale="0" id="Narr_l1zLZSH6TUWeNK3CMa1QCA">113,818,669</ix:nonFraction>, which apply weighted average fixed rate at <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_OwgFp_vI5E2XKafnnhSnew" contextRef="As_Of_3_31_2026_us-gaap_SubsequentEventTypeAxis_us-gaap_SubsequentEventMember_NGNldOqeWEKEZAkmB-73ZQ" decimals="4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentInterestRateStatedPercentage" scale="-2" id="Narr_dt3xBQ1TJ0OGtSEimY-PsA">3.25</ix:nonFraction>%.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:36pt;margin:0pt;">In the first quarter of 2026, the Group has declared a semi-annual dividend of US$<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Divide_USD_shares_bIx1MrBb80OPhGT_fNi7bA" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2026_To_3_31_2026_us-gaap_DividendsAxis_xyf_O2026H1DividendsMember_us-gaap_StatementClassOfStockAxis_dei_AdrMember_us-gaap_SubsequentEventTypeAxis_us-gaap_SubsequentEventMember_bSregRyzZ0WEZssdj7YDFQ" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:CommonStockDividendsPerShareDeclared" scale="0" id="Narr__Li47zDmn0ujl4Bk2I3Eaw">0.28</ix:nonFraction> per ADS (approximately US$<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Divide_USD_shares_bIx1MrBb80OPhGT_fNi7bA" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2026_To_3_31_2026_us-gaap_DividendsAxis_xyf_O2026H1DividendsMember_us-gaap_SubsequentEventTypeAxis_us-gaap_SubsequentEventMember_wqQaYClw40SOVzlLilWIiw" decimals="4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:CommonStockDividendsPerShareDeclared" scale="0" id="Narr__xKsivNhfkmMd9nntu2TtA">0.0467</ix:nonFraction> per ordinary share). The dividend will be payable on or about <ix:nonNumeric contextRef="Duration_1_1_2026_To_3_31_2026_us-gaap_DividendsAxis_xyf_O2026H1DividendsMember_us-gaap_SubsequentEventTypeAxis_us-gaap_SubsequentEventMember_wqQaYClw40SOVzlLilWIiw" format="ixt:date-monthname-day-year-en" name="us-gaap:DividendPayableDateToBePaidDayMonthAndYear" id="Narr_SDHj0TwAUUuqaK6GjX2VPQ">May 20, 2026</ix:nonNumeric>, to shareholders of record as of the close of business on <ix:nonNumeric contextRef="Duration_1_1_2026_To_3_31_2026_us-gaap_DividendsAxis_xyf_O2026H1DividendsMember_us-gaap_SubsequentEventTypeAxis_us-gaap_SubsequentEventMember_wqQaYClw40SOVzlLilWIiw" format="ixt:date-monthname-day-year-en" name="us-gaap:DividendsPayableDateOfRecordDayMonthAndYear" id="Narr_pTCzr1sGAEqX8sIm0svgVg">April 30, 2026</ix:nonNumeric>.</p></ix:nonNumeric></div><div style="clear:both;padding-bottom:36pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:24pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;">F-58</p></div></div>
